//! Golden-file validation against an established power-flow tool.
//!
//! Every check elsewhere in this workspace is internal: the solver against its
//! own invariants, the screen against the solve, AC against DC. Those catch a
//! great deal, but they cannot catch a shared misunderstanding — a sign
//! convention or a per-unit base that is wrong the same way everywhere. Only
//! an independent implementation can, and that is what this compares against.
//!
//! Goldens are generated by `tools/goldengen/generate.py` from pandapower
//! (BSD-3) and committed with a provenance header naming the generator, its
//! commit, the oracle and its version. A number this project reports has to be
//! traceable to a dataset version, a solver version and a code commit; a
//! golden without that header would break the chain at its first link.
//!
//! Tolerances are stated per quantity and chosen by measurement, with the
//! reasoning recorded next to them. A tolerance picked to make a test pass is
//! not a tolerance, it is a way of not knowing.
//!
//! This is a development dependency in spirit: nothing shipped reads a golden
//! file, and pandapower never appears in the Go or Rust dependency tree.

#![forbid(unsafe_code)]

pub mod document;

pub use document::{Golden, LoadError, load, load_all};
